{
  "id": "book-33",
  "checkpoint": 17,
  "title": "The Rocky Pass",
  "summary": "Paul e Clara avançam pela trilha rochosa de altitude, enfrentam ventos crescentes e ajudam um ao outro a superar uma passagem estreita.",
  "audio_url": "/audios/book-33.mp3",
  "word_count_target": 140,
  "story_en": "Paul and Clara hike higher along the exposed mountain ridge. The green forest is now far below them, replaced by sharp stones and patches of grey gravel. The morning sun warms their shoulders, but sudden gusts of wind sweep across the rocky gap.\n\nAhead, the trail narrows beside a sheer drop. Clara pauses to examine the ledge. “The path is tight here,” she calls over the roaring breeze. “Step carefully on the stable rock.”\n\nPaul moves forward slowly, keeping his body low against the incline. He reaches a secure handhold and extends his arm to assist Clara. She grasps his hand firmly and steps safely over the gap.\n\n“Great teamwork,” Clara says with relief. They stop for a brief breath, share a handful of dried fruit, and observe the peak rising directly above them.",
